###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Energy MAEs are total-energy errors in eV under a compute-constrained protocol (50 epochs at most), which is why they are far above published leaderboard values; the text does not say on which validation split the headline numbers are (the in-distribution split is implied by the efficiency section). Each value is a mean over three seeds; one run per model and data set is encoded.
# - Not encoded: the other baselines (SchNet, DimeNet++, PaiNN, TorchMD-Net, GotenNet, MACE, ICTP), whose values are in figures and the supplement (GotenNet 3.562 eV on OC20 is stated in the text, but GotenNet and ICTP are not in the registry); IS2RE results; OOD splits; force cosine similarity; per-step timings and training hours (Table 5: CliffordIP 216.6 h over 12 runs).
# - rMD17 (Table 1) gives aggregate MAEs over ten per-molecule models (CliffordIP 0.034 eV and 0.021 eV/A; FAENet 0.024 and 0.021; EquiformerV2 about 247 eV energy MAE, which the authors attribute to an uncalibrated energy head). Encoding it would need ten runs per architecture; it is left out.
# - The CliffordIP architecture row of Table 4 was not captured, so its layer and feature settings are missing. Read from the 'article in press' PDF, whose text carries a watermark; numbers should be checked against the final version.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
